useState is used to hold the state of a variable. An example below:
const [name, setName] = useState("Abiku");

PROPS vs STATE:
- Props are inputs or arguments passed to a component.
- State is the internal data managed by a component.

- Props are similar to function arguments.
- States are similar to local variables.

